  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Pt</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is a square planar complex and it can exhibit geometrical isomerism. It has two isomers, cis-platin and trans-platin. The complexes&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Zn</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mi>tetrahedral</mi></mfenced><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>and</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Pt</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>SCN</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;does not exhibit geometrical isomerism. The octahedral complex&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Pt</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>Cl</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;shows geometrical isomerism, it has two geometrical isomers cis and trans.</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>Cr</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>en</mi><msub><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is an octahedral complex,&nbsp;it is of the type&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><msub><mfenced><mi>AA</mi></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>bc</mi></math>&nbsp;and it can exhibit the geometrical isomerism.</p>",
    "image": null
  },
